  "dismissed_buckets": [
    {
      "pattern_id": "1.4",
      "bucket_label": "Pointer-keyed hash used for lookup-only or thread-local caches",
      "count": 16,
      "rationale_md": "Pack sites (soLogicCone.h NodeOfTermCacheKeyHash/DeltaCapCacheKeyHash, ctoscFilter.h tuple_hash, ctoscGlobal.h sclkCornerHash, ctscstrDesign.h tbbPtrHashCompare) re-read. soLogicCone caches are tbb::enumerable_thread_specific unordered_maps used only via find/insert (no order-sensitive iteration). ctoscFilter _mapModuleCost/_globalDelayMap are keyed lookup + priority-queue selection; no range-for over either map. ctoscGlobal sclkCornerHash feeds find/insert on float delays; collectSclkbagsOnTerm iterates stable sclkMgr bag vector, not hash iteration order. ctscstrDesign uses project tbbPtrHashCompare on concurrent_hash_map (safe adopter). Mirror include/ copies dismissed with primary sites."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "1.5",
      "bucket_label": "rand() in test/dead code or behind fixed deterministic seed",
      "count": 34,
      "rationale_md": "Production sweep: only ccdc/ctsccd/cgbased/ccdcgSolver.cc:501-549 uses rand in non-test code with srand(100) — fixed seed, equivalent-run deterministic. skewgrp/ctsSkewgroup.cc:152-155 and ctsDStest.cc are DisjointSet test mains only (fillMap from ctsDSNS::main). ctsutil/test/* and ctsui/*RandomTest.cc are test harnesses with srand(termId) or srand(0). msClustering boost::mt19937 _rand is default-constructed (fixed default seed), not time-based. No production hot-path unseeded rand reaching QoR/database sinks."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "1.6",
      "bucket_label": "srand(time(NULL)) only in dead test mains",
      "count": 2,
      "rationale_md": "Only skewgrp/ctsSkewgroup.cc:152 and skewgrp/ctsDStest.cc:150 call srand(time(NULL)), both inside fillMap used exclusively by DisjointSet benchmark/test mains — unreachable from CTS/CTO/CCD production flows."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "1.12",
      "bucket_label": "Filesystem iteration env-gated debug replay or unit test",
      "count": 8,
      "rationale_md": "fmaxLpSolverCompressedEndpoints.cc:2176/2606/2632 directory_iterator builds modelFilenames/baselineFilenames/child folders without sort; order could affect chained LP solves, but entry is only via FMAX_LP_FILE_FLOW / FMAX_LP_LIST_FILE_FLOW / FMAX_LP_FILE_FLOW_ICG in fmaxLpSolver.cc:98-137 (debug file-replay; env control surface out of scope per triage brief). ctsutil/ctsTest.cc:985/1646 readdir loops are test harness. Not promoted without production trigger."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "3.1",
      "bucket_label": "parallel_reduce boolean early-exit — associative/latent (prior C4)",
      "count": 2,
      "rationale_md": "ctomtGlsProblemGenerator.h:312 runSccIteration uses tbb::parallel_reduce with std::atomic<bool> globalDone and reduceAnd/reduceOr on bool accumulators under execPolicy::MultiThread when sccVec.size() >= large_skew_group_limit_for_threading. Re-verified: bodies write local acc only; final AND/OR is schedule-insensitive; only localLog string order varies (diagnostic). Prior MT report C4 verdict stands — latent-only, not REAL HIGH/MEDIUM."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "3.2",
      "bucket_label": "MT concurrent containers — idempotent, canonicalized, or accessor-serialized (prior C2/C3/C7/C9)",
      "count": 80,
      "rationale_md": "Pack-wide 3.2 hits are predominantly declared tbb::concurrent_* types plus parallel_for sites. Deep re-read of hot writers: insertDrcToCache (C9) uses concurrent_hash_map accessor per termId — latent idempotent; processSccBagIntoCache (C3) disjoint bags + assemble canonicalizes; ctoCGLat::getPhaseDelay _phaseDelays (C2) under exclusive cgLatMapMT accessor — latent idempotent; ctsInterClockBalance concurrent_vector→std::set median (C7) neutralized. Remaining pack entries are parallel_for job dispatch without proven divergent shared mutation reaching QoR. No REAL HIGH/MEDIUM promoted."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "3.5",
      "bucket_label": "hardware_concurrency sets TBB grain only (prior C5 false positive)",
      "count": 3,
      "rationale_md": "ctoGrpLatCalc.cc:80 uses std::thread::hardware_concurrency() only to compute _step grain for blocked_range; each worker writes unique grpLat[idx[i]]. ctsMtTaskRunner.h:81 uses tbb::this_task_arena::max_concurrency() for arena sizing, not host HW thread count. Schedule-only; prior MT C5 re-verified — false positive for equivalent-run ND."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "4.1",
      "bucket_label": "Lazy mutable _termValidSclkCache — MT-unreachable (prior C1)",
      "count": 2,
      "rationale_md": "ctsInfra.h:838 mutable dosMap _termValidSclkCache filled in isTermValidForSclk/getTermValidSclks (ctsInfra.cc:7034-7074). Comment claims thread-safe but no lock. Caller sweep: checkValidCandidate/getTermValidSclks on GLS seed path (findNextProblem/spinOffSeed/selectSeedCandidate*) runs sequentially before MT workers; addTermsToUpTermsMapOfGrpTerm iterates std::set<ctsSclk> sclkValSetType (deterministic order). No call from runSccIteration/populateSharedSccCache worker bodies on shared ctsInfra. Prior MT C1 dead/unused for MT ND — re-verified."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "4.2",
      "bucket_label": "ST lazy first-touch size()==0 guards — not MT race shapes",
      "count": 38,
      "rationale_md": "Pack 4.2 sites (soSolverUpdater, soPredictiveCcd, msCstrDesign, soDesign, soClockGate, ms* modules, ctsRouteMgr, etc.) are classic lazy populate-on-first-use in sequential const methods or single-threaded flow init. msPreserveSentinel.h mutex entries are safe-adopter, not defects. No site proved concurrent first-touch on shared mutable state without TBB accessor/lock reaching divergent QoR under equivalent-run MT."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "4.4",
      "bucket_label": "concurrent_hash_map / check-then-act — serialized or latent (prior C2/C3/C9)",
      "count": 36,
      "rationale_md": "Pack 4.4 enumerates concurrent_hash_map and concurrent_unordered_* declarations plus ctomtGlsProblemGenerator sharedSccCache.processedBags check-then-act. Re-verified: QoR-path writers (insertDrcToCache, getPhaseDelay, processSccBagIntoCache) either hold TBB accessors, use concurrent containers with idempotent values, or rely on disjoint-key invariants documented at assemble time. ctscstrDesign threadSafeDesignObserverHash uses tbbPtrHashCompare. No proven divergent check-then-act outcome on REAL HIGH/MEDIUM paths."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "hot-suspect",
      "bucket_label": "Known hot suspects — all re-verified non-promotable",
      "count": 8,
      "rationale_md": "skewgrp/ctsSkewgroup.cc srand(time)+rand: test main only. ccdc/ccdcgSolver.cc srand(100)+rand: fixed seed, deterministic. soLogicCone.h std::hash<const void*>: thread-local lookup caches. ctoscFilter.h/ctoscGlobal.h pointer hashes: membership/lookup only. fmaxLpSolverCompressedEndpoints.cc directory_iterator: env-gated debug file flow. ctomtGlsProblemGenerator.h parallel_reduce: latent C4. ctoGrpLatCalc.cc hardware_concurrency: false positive C5. ctsInfra.h _termValidSclkCache: MT-unreachable C1."
    },
    {
      "pattern_id": "prior-mt",
      "bucket_label": "Prior MT report C1-C10 re-verification — none elevated",
      "count": 10,
      "rationale_md": "Re-read cts_nd_details.md outcomes against local source: C1/C10 dead/unused MT; C2/C3/C4/C6/C8/C9 latent-only (race-idempotent, canonicalized-after-join, or FP association); C5 false positive; C7 neutralized. Strongest concurrent writer remains insertDrcToCache (C9) but still idempotent under accessor protocol — not promoted to REAL HIGH/MEDIUM."
    }
  ]
